OTHER INFORMATION IN THIS LIBRARY.

This example DOES NOT include a mechanism for generating the timing,
verilog, or lef files from the included layouts and/or schematics.
Any or all of these tools must be requested separately from Micro
Magic and will only be provided once the tools have been purchased
from Micro Magic and then (some of them) for additional cost.


Installation:
==============

SUE DPC:

The file:

	mmi25/library/dpc/dpc.suerc

contains all of the SUE startup data required to run DPC with this
example.  The first line of this file must be edited to include the
correct complete pathname to this installation.  Furthermore, if you
want to run Primetime, instead of Pearl, you must uncomment out the
line:

	#set DPC_TIMING(simulator) "primetime"

This file must be sourced when you start up SUE.  This can be done in
a number of ways.  One way is to add the lines:

        set tech <dir>
	source $tech/library/dpc/dpc.suerc

to the .suerc file in $MMI_TOOLS/../mmi_local/sue/.suerc or to your
home or current directory .suerc files.  Alternatively, you can add
the following lines:

	switch [use_first PROJECT env(PROJECT)] {
	  mmi25 {
	    set tech <dir>
	    source $tech/library/dpc/dpc.suerc
	    puts "Setting up for DPC with mmi25 library ..."
	  }
	}

to $MMI_TOOLS/../mmi_local/sue/.suerc or similar.  With this, you
can load the DPC example by either invoking SUE by:

	sue -SET PROJECT=mmi25

or by setting the UNIX environment variable PROJECT to mmi25, e.g.:

	setenv PROJECT mmi25

and then simply invoking SUE with:

	sue


Example Circuit:

A very simple example circuit, alu8, is also included.  Try running
"dpc it" or "dpc netlist" on it.
